plan.html:83:   <p>airways.gg has no programmatic API — all data flows through SvelteKit load functions. When an agent needs to debug a data issue (wrong flight status, missing weather, scraper gap), there is no way to query the database except a direct Postgres connection. The debug API adds a Bearer-token-gated /api/debug/* route group with structured table endpoints, UI-parity mirrors that reuse existing query functions, and a SELECT-only raw SQL escape hatch. Auth is a ~10-line addition to hooks.server.ts... [truncated]
plan.html:89:   <p>An agent can GET /api/debug/flights?date=2026-06-07&amp;status=delayed&amp;limit=50 to query flights, GET /api/debug/ui/homepage to get the exact data the homepage renders, GET /api/debug/ui/stats?range=30 for stats dashboard data, and POST /api/debug/sql with {"sql": "SELECT ..."} for ad-hoc queries. All endpoints return JSON with row counts and query timing. All are gated behind Authorization: Bearer &lt;DEBUG_API_TOKEN&gt;. Raw SQL is SELECT-only.</p>
